# sudoku

Sunlit Sudoku — a zero-dependency, framework-free 9x9 Sudoku web game with pencil notes, hints, peer/number highlighting, a rainbow palette, light/dark themes, per-difficulty best times, and PWA install, live at games.beric.ca/sudoku.

## TL;DR

- **What:** "Sunlit Sudoku" — a single-page 9x9 Sudoku game with three built-in puzzles (easy / medium / hard), pencil notes, hints, peer + same-number highlighting, a rainbow cell palette, light/dark themes, and best-time tracking per difficulty. Installable as a PWA.
- **How:** Pure vanilla HTML/CSS/JS — no framework, no build step for the game itself. The solution and the three puzzle layouts are hard-coded in `app.js`; state persists in `localStorage`.
- **Stack:** Vanilla JS · HTML · CSS · PWA (`manifest.webmanifest` + `service-worker.js`) · bun + `sharp` for the icon build script.
- **Run it:** `bunx serve .` then open the printed localhost URL (a server is needed for the service worker / PWA to work).
- **Deploy:** `bun run deploy` → Cloudflare Pages project `games-portal`, live at **https://games.beric.ca/sudoku/**.

## Overview

A self-contained browser Sudoku game with no framework and no bundler. The board, the single correct `SOLUTION`, and the easy/medium/hard `PUZZLES` are all defined directly in `app.js`. Gameplay features:

- **Pencil notes** — toggle candidate digits per cell.
- **Hints** — reveal a correct value.
- **Highlighting** — peers (row/column/box) and all cells sharing the selected number light up.
- **Rainbow palette** — per-cell color accents.
- **Themes** — light and dark.
- **Best times** — tracked per difficulty, persisted in `localStorage`.
- **PWA** — installable and offline-capable via a service worker scoped to `/sudoku/`.

## Tech Stack

| Layer | Technology |
|-------|-----------|
| Game | Vanilla HTML / CSS / JS (`index.html`, `app.js`, `styles.css`) — no framework, no build step |
| PWA | `manifest.webmanifest`, `service-worker.js` (scope + `start_url` = `/sudoku/`) |
| Tooling | bun runs `scripts/build-icons.mjs`; `sharp` generates the PWA icons |
| Hosting | Cloudflare Pages — project `games-portal`, domain `games.beric.ca` |

## Project Layout

```
index.html / app.js / styles.css   # game source (repo root = dev copy)
package.json                       # bun scripts: build:icons, deploy
scripts/
  build-icons.mjs                  # generates PWA icons via sharp
  deploy.sh                        # deploys deploy/ to Cloudflare Pages
  list-deployments.sh              # lists recent Pages deployments
deploy/                            # what actually ships to games.beric.ca
  index.html                       # games portal landing page  ->  /
  sudoku/                          # the Sudoku app              ->  /sudoku/
```

The `games.beric.ca` Pages project is a multi-game portal: the landing page is served at `/` and this game is mounted at `/sudoku/`.

## Getting Started

```bash
bunx serve .        # serve the repo root, open the localhost URL
bun install         # only needed for the icon script (sharp)
bun run build:icons # regenerate PWA icons
```

## Scripts

| Command | What it does |
|---------|--------------|
| `bun run build:icons` | Generate `icon-192.png`, `icon-512.png`, `apple-touch-icon.png` via sharp |
| `bun run deploy` | Deploy `deploy/` to Cloudflare Pages (production, branch=main) |
| `./scripts/deploy.sh preview` | Preview-branch deploy |
| `./scripts/list-deployments.sh` | List recent Pages deployments |

## Deployment (Cloudflare Pages)

`deploy.sh` deploys the `deploy/` directory to the Cloudflare Pages project `games-portal` via `wrangler pages deploy`. On each deploy it copies `deploy/` to a temp build dir and:

- appends `?v=<git-short-sha>` to local CSS/JS refs in every HTML file (browser cache-bust), and
- stamps the service-worker cache version (`__SW_VERSION__` → SHA) so the PWA cache invalidates per release.

Credentials: the script reads the Cloudflare Global API Key from `~/Arik/dev/.env`.

> **Sync gotcha (load-bearing):** when editing the game, update **both** the root copies **and** `deploy/sudoku/` (`index.html`, `app.js`, `styles.css`) — they must stay in sync. Only the `deploy/` tree ships; the repo root is the dev/working copy.

## Status

Live and playable in production at **https://games.beric.ca/sudoku/**. The puzzles are a fixed built-in set (easy/medium/hard derived from one hard-coded solution) — there is no puzzle generator. No test suite; the game is verified by playing it in the browser.
